# Keeps `npx expo install` working.
#
# npx exports the global ~/.npmrc `allow-scripts` list into the environment as
# npm_config_allow_scripts. Expo's spawned `npm install` inherits it, and npm 11+
# treats an env-supplied value the same as the `--allow-scripts` CLI flag, which
# it forbids in project-scoped installs — so every `npx expo install` died with
# EALLOWSCRIPTS. Clearing it here overrides the inherited value.
#
# This does not weaken anything: the `allowScripts` field in package.json is the
# real authority for this project, and npm ignores .npmrc's list when that field
# is present. Add new postinstall-script allowances there, not here.
allow-scripts=
